  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 321 PM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nThe before mentioned cold front will drift south into northern \nKansas Monday, before lifting north as a warm front Monday \nnight. Cooler temps are expected for Monday with highs in the \n80s to near 90 in SW Nebraska. After dry conditions Monday, the \nthreat for precipitation will increase Monday evening as the \nnortherly moving warm front interacts with a decent mid level \ndisturbance lifting northeast from Colorado. The upper level \npattern will shift somewhat midweek as a trough of low pressure \napproaches the west coast. This will force upper level high \npressure east into the Ohio Valley. Resultant low amplitude west\nsouthwest mid level flow and a surface front, meandering across\nthe forecast area, will lead to a continued threat for \nthunderstorms during the afternoon and evening hours Tuesday and\nWednesday. High pressure will retrograde west into the four \ncorners Friday into Saturday. Ridging will extend north into the\nnorthern Rockies, further limiting precipitation chances Friday\ninto Saturday. Highs will be in the 90s Friday with upper 80s \nand lower 90s for Saturday.",
